<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia posts 1.03 percent inflation in January.</title>
<headline>Indonesia posts 1.03 percent inflation in January.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's consumer price index rose 1.03 percent month-on-month in January, compared with 0.55 percent in December, Information Minister Harmoko on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Harmoko said increases in the price of food and services were responsible for the rise in consumer price index.</p>
<p>			  Jan	Dec	Jan 96</p>
<p>    Month/month    +1.03    +0.55     +2.16</p>
<p>    Year/year	+5.34    +6.47     +9.64</p>
<p>CPI sectors (month/month)</p>
<p>    Food	     +1.85    +1.28     +4.48</p>
<p>    Housing	  +0.25    +0.05     +0.77</p>
<p>    Textiles	 +0.58    +0.46     +1.75</p>
<p>    Services	 +0.92    +0.08     +1.08</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
